### MiniPlayer.jsx: re-enable unmuted autoplay (Mac/iOS app only)

File: `frontend/src/components/MiniPlayer.jsx`

This change is intentionally NOT shipped on the Linux prep branch because
it would break the live PWA: browsers (Safari, Chrome, Firefox) block
unmuted autoplay, so `autoplay=1` without `mute=1` produces a paused
iframe while our React state thinks it's playing. The user would tap the
play button and our handler would call `pauseVideo` because `playing` is
already true. State desync.

The change is safe ONLY inside WKWebView with
`config.mediaTypesRequiringUserActionForPlayback = []` (see
CustomViewController.swift). Apply it on the Mac, in the same commit as
the iOS project, so the two ship together.

---

Around line 75–76, restore initial state to autoplay-friendly defaults:

    -  const [muted, setMuted]         = useState(false);
    -  const [playing, setPlaying]     = useState(false);
    +  const [muted, setMuted]         = useState(false);
    +  const [playing, setPlaying]     = useState(true);

(`muted` is already `false`; only `playing` needs to flip to `true`.)

Around line 403–406, restore autoplay in the embed URL:

    -  const src =
    -    `https://www.youtube.com/embed/${videoId}` +
    -    `?playsinline=1&rel=0&modestbranding=1&fs=0` +
    -    `&cc_load_policy=0&iv_load_policy=3&controls=0&enablejsapi=1`;
    +  // autoplay=1 without mute=1 works here because WKWebView is configured
    +  // with mediaTypesRequiringUserActionForPlayback = [] in
    +  // CustomViewController.swift. Do NOT ship this change to the live PWA —
    +  // regular browsers will block it and the React state will desync from
    +  // the iframe state.
    +  const src =
    +    `https://www.youtube.com/embed/${videoId}` +
    +    `?autoplay=1&playsinline=1&rel=0&modestbranding=1&fs=0` +
    +    `&cc_load_policy=0&iv_load_policy=3&controls=0&enablejsapi=1`;

